    "chunk_text": "ICC Port City (Private) Limited. seeks to carry out the objectives of residential development, driving investment in the CPC, expansion of ICC's existing project portfolio, catering to international markets, conduct sales and marketing activities to sell apartments and to engage with foreign investors with the goal of attracting required foreign investment. ICC Port City (Private) Limited. will also offer the core services of luxury apartments, luxury villas and commercial space for sale or rent as well as serviced apartments and management services extending to rental management services and condominium management services.\n\nICC Port City (Private) Limited. will invest USD 66,000,000 and LKR 13,800,000,000 to commence the business being carried out from Colombo Port City. This amount includes expenses for the land and development cost of the project.\n\nIn engaging in this business, ICC Port City (Private) Limited. will recruit 8 direct employees employed locally in the first year and this is to increase to 12 direct employees by the fourth year of operations. ICC Port City (Private) Limited. will also recruit 343 indirect employees in the first year and this is to increase to 862 indirect employees by the fourth year to engage in design, engineering and construction.\n\nThe project's alignment with the Port City\u2019s growth potential and its favourable business climate enables ICC Port City (Private) Limited. to position itself as a premier player in Sri Lanka\u2019s evolving luxury real estate market enhancing both the company\u2019s and the country\u2019s global market presence.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'07'14Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.07.20254A\n\nSCHEDULE III\n\nExemptions or Incentives granted under the Enactments\n\nEnactments listed underSchedule II of the ActExemptions or incentives grante