    "chunk_text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'07'14Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 14.07.2025\n\n3A\n\nSCHEDULE II\n\nRationale for the Consideration of the Primary Business of Strategic Importance\n\nClothespin Management and Development (Private) Limited., incorporated in Sri Lanka, is poised to develop a definitive artistic and architectural icon in the name of Clothespin Towers in Colombo Port City, this will attract the world's most prestigious investors, global influencers and high-profile companies. Clothespin Towers is strategically designed to cater to high-value market segments residential, hospitality and commercial positioning itself as a landmark investment in Sri Lanka's booming real estate and tourism industry.\n\nClothespin Management and Development (Private) Limited. aims to develop a twin tower marvel that will seamlessly integrate luxury residencies, a seven-star hotel, high end retail spaces and elite office environments, all while housing the world's largest art gallery in the Hotel Use Land Plot 2-01-11 spanning over an area of 24,324 sqm in Colombo Port City.\n\nThe Clothespin twin-tower development features ultra-luxury residences, a seven-star hotel, fine-dining restaurants, premium retail spaces, infinity pools, wellness centers and high-tech office spaces. Designed for LEED Gold Certification, the project integrates smart building systems, energy-efficient infrastructure, solar power, rainwater harvesting and automated climate control.\n\nClothespin Management and Development (Private) Limited. intends to invest a total investment of USD 540,104,317 with an allocation of USD 75,000,000 for land lease and USD 465,104,317 for construction costs and pre-operative expenses in Colombo Port City and will recruit 280 employees in the first year."
